      "id": "pipeline",
      "text": "Here is how it works. First, your documents are split into chunks and converted into vector embeddings. These vectors are stored in a database. When a user asks a question, the query gets embedded too. A similarity search finds the most relevant chunks. Those chunks are injected into the prompt alongside the question. The LLM reads the evidence, then answers.",
